  "visualBrief": "Merowe Dam’s west and east embankments, central spillway with twelve low sluices and two surface gates, angled intake dam, ten domed turbine housings, powerhouse and immediate service structures.",
  "heightPolicy": "Absolute mean-sea-level placement fixes the modeled crest at 303 m. The design full pool is 300 m. With the retained PMTiles shorelines and standard Terrarium terrain, the runtime water sampler gives 252.43–271.86 m in central reservoir tiles and 250.22–255.31 m in the tailwater. Changing the terrain provider does not move the dam.",
  "nativeAxes": "+X east, +Z south. The crest bends across the north edge of the concrete river crossing. The Nile flows from the reservoir on local -Z toward the tailwater on local +Z.",
